---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_DATA } from '../constants';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';

import '../styles/about.css';
---

<Layout pageTitle="About">
    <div class="page-container">
        <h1>About me</h1>

        <div class="about-content">
            <div class="about-intro-wrapper centered-column">
                <div class="about-header centered-column">
                    <Portrait alt={SITE_DATA.name} class="about-portrait" sizes="120px" />
                    <h2 class="about-name">{SITE_DATA.name}</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="intro-text">
                    Since 2015 I am a <a href="https://www.cwts.nl/people/vincent-traag" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">senior researcher</a>
                    at the <a href="https://www.cwts.nl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Centre for Science and Technology Studies (CWTS)</a>
                    of <a href="https://www.leidenuniv.nl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Leiden University</a> in the Netherlands.
                    I am coordinating our <a href="https://www.cwts.nl/research/focal-areas/engagement-inclusion" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Focal Area of Engagement &amp; Inclusion</a>
                    and am leading the flagship project on science in societal contention. In addition to my scientific
                    research, I am also a bibliometric consultant at CWTS.
                </p>
            </div>

            <section>
                <h2>Research</h2>
                <div class="info-card">
                    <p>
                        My main interests are mathematical models in the social sciences with a focus on (social)
                        networks, including topics such as complex networks, social influence (as in opinion dynamics
                        and the like), and conflict. In particular, I am interested in how science and society interact
                        on contentious issues. These are research topics where hopefully math can meet the social sciences.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Research Interests</h2>
                <ul class="custom-list">
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Science and society</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">How science and society interact on contentious issues,
                        including science in societal contention, misinformation, and engagement &amp; inclusion in research.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Complex networks</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Methods for detecting communities in complex networks, such as the
                        <a href="https://github.com/vtraag/leidenalg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Leiden algorithm</a>,
                        applied across the (social) sciences, from citation networks to international relations.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Social influence and conflict</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Mathematical models of social influence, opinion dynamics,
                        reputation and conflict.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Science studies and research evaluation</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Scientometrics, research assessment and the use of metrics,
                        studied with causal and quantitative methods.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Positions</h2>
                <ul class="work-list icon-list">
                    <li>
                        <div class="list-entry">
                            <h3>Senior researcher</h3>
                            <p class="institution">Centre for Science and Technology Studies (CWTS), Leiden University, 2015–present</p>
                            <p>Coordinator of the Focal Area of Engagement &amp; Inclusion, leading the flagship project
                            on science in societal contention, and bibliometric consultant.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Education</h2>
                <ul class="education-list icon-list">
                    <li>
                        <div class="education-entry">
                            <h3>PhD in Applied Mathematics</h3>
                            <p class="institution"><a href="https://uclouvain.be" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Université catholique de Louvain</a>, Louvain-la-Neuve, Belgium, 2013</p>
                            <p class="grade">Thesis: <a href="http://hdl.handle.net/2078.1/134615" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">"Algorithms and dynamical models for communities and reputation in social networks"</a>.
                            During my PhD I studied methods for detecting communities in complex networks, resulting in a
                            <a href="https://github.com/vtraag/leidenalg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Python software package</a>.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <div class="education-entry">
                            <h3>MSc in Sociology</h3>
                            <p class="institution"><a href="https://www.uva.nl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">University of Amsterdam</a>, 2008</p>
                            <p class="grade">Cum laude. Thesis: <a href="http://dare.uva.nl/en/scriptie/273167" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">"Popularity Distributions with Social Influence"</a>.
                            Coming from a computer science background, I took up mathematics during my studies in sociology.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>Contact</h2>
                <p>
                    You can probably best reach me through e-mail at
                    <a href={`mailto:${SITE_DATA.email}`}>{SITE_DATA.email}</a>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    For security, you can use my
                    <a href="https://keys.openpgp.org/search?q=0x6727C61107D0C6F0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PGP key</a>
                    (fingerprint <code>42FE F12E E258 76A2 1926 49AA 6727 C611 07D0 C6F0</code>); details are also on
                    <a href="https://keybase.io/vtraag" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Keybase</a>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Visiting address:</strong>
                    <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/search?query=Kolffpad%201%2C%20Leiden" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Office B5.31, CWTS, Willem Einthoven Building, Kolffpad 1, 2333 BN Leiden</a>, the Netherlands<br />
                    <strong>Postal address:</strong> CWTS, Leiden University, P.O. Box 905, 2300 AX Leiden, the Netherlands<br />
                    <strong>Telephone:</strong> <a href="tel:+31715273943">+31 (0)71 527 3943</a>
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
